course: dictionary
lesson: 8115
title: Repaint and the clue re-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can be a clue. Re- often means again, so repaint is paint plus re-, which means to paint again. «Repaint the fence» means paint the fence once more, perhaps because the old paint is worn or you want a new colour.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «That is still copying, the way repainting your mate's bike doesn't make it your bike.» If repainting means painting again, the sentence makes sense: a new coat of paint does not change who owns the bike.
explain: Repaint also turns up in maths problems. You might work out the area to repaint on a fence, then how many tins of paint you need. «Freshly repainted» tells you the surface has just had a new coat.
fact: Repaint means to paint something again, usually in a new colour or because the old paint is worn.
fact: The prefix re- means again, so reread, rewrite and repaint all mean do something once more.
fact: «Repaint the fence» means paint the fence again.
fact: «Freshly repainted» means painted again very recently.
fact: Repaint is a verb: repaint, repaints, repainted, repainting.
exercise: «We will repaint the fence this weekend.» What does repaint mean here? | To buy a new fence | To take down | To wash with water | *To paint again
exercise: In repaint, the part re- means what? | Not | *Again | Before | Under
exercise: «The bench was freshly repainted, so the paint was still wet.» What does freshly repainted suggest? | Broken and thrown away | *Painted again very recently | Old and never touched | Covered in mud for years
test: Why might you repaint a bike? | To hide it from your mates | *To give it a new colour or cover worn paint | To make it heavier to ride
test: Which part of repaint means again? | *re | paint | pain | tin
exam: Dan says repainting his mate's bike makes it his own. What does «That is still copying, the way repainting your mate's bike doesn't make it your bike» show? | *Painting again does not change who owns something | Copying is always fair | Repainting always changes the owner | Bikes cannot be painted at all
